<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- The page shell — one markup tree, two layouts. Wide: `#drawer` is the
     conversation column beside the chat, its header hidden. Narrow: `#drawer`
     is a full-screen overlay the `#topbar` menu button opens, and `#topbar` is
     what is hidden the other way round. Nothing here is per-device: the split
     is media queries in style.css, so resizing a window crosses it live.
     See DECISIONS.md D_one_shell_two_layouts.

     Server-rendered snapshot of the transcript and status bar; public/app.js
     then connects an EventSource and applies deltas. Block divs are addressed
     by their transcript id — the SSE `block` event upserts by id, `remove`
     deletes by id.

     `data-theme` carries the resolved `theme` cookie so the first paint is
     already in the right palette; the toggle's label names the theme it
     switches *to*, and app.js keeps both in sync after a click.

     `data-conversation` names what this tab is showing. It is also what the
     EventSource subscribes to, so the server sends this tab only its own
     conversation's frames — a turn running elsewhere never arrives here.

     `interactive-widget=resizes-content` is what keeps the composer above
     iOS's on-screen keyboard instead of behind it. -->
<html lang="en" data-theme="<%= theme %>" data-conversation="<%= conversation %>">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, interactive-widget=resizes-content">
  <title><%= title %> · pikuri-web</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <!-- The conversation column, and the phone's drawer. The chrome sits *around*
       the nav rather than inside it: GET /conversations replaces the nav's
       innerHTML on every list change, and anything in there would need event
       delegation plus a theme-cookie read in that route. -->
  <div id="drawer">
    <header id="drawer-header">
      <button type="button" id="drawer-close" aria-label="Close the conversation list">&times;</button>
    </header>

    <nav id="sidebar" aria-label="Conversations"><%==
      erb(:_sidebar, layout: false, locals: { conversations: conversations })
    %></nav>

    <!-- Starting a conversation belongs with the list of conversations. It also
         has to live somewhere the phone can reach with the status bar stripped
         to one line of text — and duplicating these per layout would mean
         duplicate ids. -->
    <footer id="drawer-footer">
      <button type="button" id="new-conversation" class="flat-button"
              title="Start a fresh conversation">+ new conversation</button>
      <button type="button" id="theme-toggle" class="flat-button"
              title="Switch to the <%= theme == 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark' %> theme"
              aria-label="Switch to the <%= theme == 'dark' ? 'light' : 'dark' %> theme"><%=
        theme == 'dark' ? '☀ light' : '☾ dark'
      %></button>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <div id="chat">
    <header id="topbar">
      <button type="button" id="drawer-open" aria-label="Show the conversation list"
              aria-expanded="false">&#9776;</button>
      <span id="topbar-title"><%= title %></span>
    </header>

    <main id="transcript">
      <% blocks.each do |block| %>
      <div class="block <%= block.kind %>" id="<%= block.id %>"><%== block.html %></div>
      <% end %>
    </main>

    <!-- Send and stop stay two buttons: sending mid-turn injects, so an arrow
         that becomes a stop square while busy would cost the injection
         (D_interloper_mid_loop_input). The stop button appears beside it.

         The composer precedes the status bar, as on the desktop it always has;
         the phone layout swaps them with `order` rather than a DOM reshuffle. -->
    <form id="composer">
      <input type="hidden" name="conversation" value="<%= conversation %>">
      <!-- The hint is a title, not the placeholder: a paragraph of placeholder
           wraps to three lines in a phone-width composer, and Chrome sizes an
           empty textarea to its wrapped placeholder, so app.js's auto-grow
           opens the box at three lines before a character is typed. -->
      <textarea name="prompt" id="prompt" rows="1" autofocus placeholder="Message…"
                title="Enter to send, Shift+Enter for newline; sending mid-turn injects"></textarea>
      <button type="submit" id="send" aria-label="Send" title="Send">&#8593;</button>
      <button type="button" id="cancel" aria-label="Stop this turn" title="Stop this turn"
              <%= 'hidden' unless status[:busy] %>>&#9632;</button>
    </form>

    <footer id="status-bar">
      <span id="status-state"><%= status[:state] == :queued ? 'waiting for a free slot' : status[:state] %></span>
      <span id="status-pending"><%= status[:pending].positive? ? "#{status[:pending]} queued" : '' %></span>
      <span id="status-tokens"><%= status[:tokens] %></span>
    </footer>
  </div>

  <script src="/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
